## Section 1 — Cost rules (mandatory query shape)

### 1.1  Partition / cluster filters (mandatory on listed tables)

| Table | Partition | Cluster | Rule |
|-------|-----------|---------|------|
| **`inventory_master`** (7.2B rows, 650 GB) | `date` | `store_code` | **ALWAYS add `WHERE date BETWEEN ...`**. Ideally `store_code IN (...)` too. |
| **`transaction_master`** (389M rows, 73 GB) | `date` | `channel` | Add `WHERE date BETWEEN ...` for any query not intentionally full-history. |
| `anaplan_transit_calender_cleaned` (51M rows) | `Datestring` | — | Add `WHERE Datestring BETWEEN ...` |
| `anaplan_allocation_calendar_cleaned` | — | `SKU_ID` | Filter/join on `SKU_ID` for cluster pruning |
| `anaplan_fdod_alloc_cleaned` | — | `SKU_ID` | Same |
| `assortment_plan_cleaned` | — | `SKU_ID` | Same |
| `transfer_orders_new_cleaned` | — | `sku_id` | Same |

**Exception**: metadata queries (`__TABLES__`, `INFORMATION_SCHEMA`) don't need filters.

### 1.2  Default `LIMIT` for exploratory queries

When sampling/exploring (not aggregating), always add `LIMIT 100` (or smaller) until you've seen the shape. Never `SELECT *` from a partitioned big table without both a date filter *and* a `LIMIT`.

