## Section 3 — Reference: sentinels, quirks, dirty columns

### 3.1  Sentinels

| Sentinel | Type | Where | How to catch |
|---|---|---|---|
| `\N` (literal 2-char string) | STRING | `product_master.gender`, `assortment_plan_cleaned.PLANNING_STYLE_OPTION`, others | `IS NULL OR col = '\N' OR col = ''` (`IS NULL` alone misses it) |
| `''` (empty) | STRING | Various | Same as above |
| `9999-12-31` | DATE/STRING | `price_book.EFFECTIVE_TO_DAY_ID` | "Open-ended" / valid-forever marker |

### 3.2  100%-zero / 100%-null columns in `transaction_master` (do not model on these)

`line_id`, `launch_price`, `transaction_type`, `fullfilment_location_customer` (typo in column name), `revenue_before_tax`, `ship_to_country`, `freight_cost`, `store_contribution`, `workstream`, `currency_exchange_rate`, `order_type`, `transaction_category`, `cost`, `msrp`, `unit_discount_amount`, `total_discount_amount`, `clearance`, `clearance_price`, `flagged_rows`.

Most are hardcoded NULL/0 in the master-build DDL — see [`findings/raw_to_master_lineage.md`](findings/raw_to_master_lineage.md) Section 4.

### 3.3  `transaction_master` zero-qty rows

~27% of rows have `qty = 0 AND revenue = 0 AND price = 0`. **For real-sales modeling, filter `WHERE qty > 0 AND revenue > 0`.**

