## Section 4 — SQL gotchas (numbered, fixed-shape)

> **Template for any new gotcha** (the META-RULE in Section 0.1 enforces this shape):
> ```
> ### Gn. <one-line title>
>
> **Error signature:** `<copy-pasteable substring of the error>`
> **Root cause:** <one sentence>
> **Fix:**
> | Don't | Do |
> |---|---|
> | … | … |
> **Burned on:** queries/<file>.sql (line N), <date>
> ```

### G1. Reserved keywords cannot be used as column aliases

**Error signature:** `Syntax error: Unexpected keyword ROWS` (or RANGE, GROUPS, ORDER, PARTITION, OVER, WINDOW, QUALIFY, INTERVAL, HASH, LOOKUP, TABLESAMPLE, MERGE, STRUCT, ARRAY, EXCEPT, INTERSECT, UNION).
**Root cause:** Many BQ keywords are forbidden as bare aliases; the error surfaces at the *reference* site (e.g. another CTE), not the definition.
**Fix:** never use these as bare aliases. If you must, backtick: `` AS `rows` ``.

| Don't | Do |
|---|---|
| `AS rows` | `AS row_count` |
| `AS range` | `AS value_range` |
| `AS order` | `AS sort_order` or `AS ord` |
| `AS groups` | `AS group_count` |
| `AS type` | `AS type_name` (usually safe but err on caution) |

### G2. Numeric-looking columns in raw tables are often STRING

**Error signature:** `No matching signature for operator = for argument types: STRING, INT64`
**Root cause:** Many `*_cleaned*` raw tables store numeric values as `STRING`, including blank strings and `'\N'` sentinels.
**Fix:** always `SAFE_CAST(col AS FLOAT64)` (or `INT64`) when doing math, aggregation, or numeric comparison on raw tables. Known offenders listed in Section 3.5.
**Burned on:** multiple — this is a class of error, not a single instance.

### G3. `__TABLES__` uses `table_id`, not `table_name`

**Error signature:** `Name table_name not found inside t`
**Root cause:** Legacy `<dataset>.__TABLES__` exposes `table_id`, `row_count`, `size_bytes`, `creation_time`, `last_modified_time`, `type`. The newer `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES` exposes `table_name`. Mixing the two (e.g. in a `UNION ALL`) trips the error.
**Fix:** pick one API and stick with it per query.

### G4. Multi-level aggregation needs a `GROUP BY` modifier

**Error signature:** `Multi-level aggregation requires the enclosing aggregate function to have one or more GROUP BY modifiers`
**Root cause:** Nesting aggregates inline (e.g. `ARRAY_AGG(COUNT(*) OVER ...)` or `SUM(COUNT(*))` without grouping).
**Fix:** split into two CTEs — inner CTE does the first aggregation with explicit `GROUP BY`, outer query aggregates over the CTE.

### G5. String-sentinel check on a non-STRING column

**Error signature:** `No matching signature for operator =` (when comparing INT64/FLOAT64 to `''` or `'\N'`)
**Root cause:** `'`, `'\N'`, and friends only make sense on STRING columns.
**Fix:**

| Column type | Null/sentinel check |
|---|---|
| STRING | `IS NULL OR col = '' OR col = '\N'` |
| INT64 / FLOAT64 | `IS NULL` (plus `= 0` if zero is also a sentinel) |
| Defensive (unknown type) | See G10 |

### G6. _(promoted to Section 0.4 practice note — `SELECT DISTINCT *` is a grain-bug smell, not an error.)_

### G7. _(merged into G1 — backtick when in doubt.)_

